      "content": "Individuals from East Asian backgrounds are often characterized by a tendency for high levels of conscientiousness, marked by diligence and self-discipline. They typically display a strong preference for social harmony and may prioritize collective success over individual achievement, which aids them in high-stress professional settings. Middle Eastern individuals often exhibit a high degree of extraversion and may use emotions and interpersonal connectivity as a strategy to cope with pressure. They tend to value community support, which can be a source of resilience in demanding environments.",
